{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-149419",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "Using the hint, the volume of the solid generated when the region bounded by a curve $y=f(x),$ the $x$-axis, and the vertical lines $x=0$ and $x=15$ is rotated $2\\pi $ radians about the $x$-axis is given by\n\n$$\nV=\\pi {\\int }_{0}^{15}[f(x)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nLet $g(x)={(f(x))}^{2}.$ The (regular) step size $Δx$ is given by \n\n$$\nΔx=\\frac{15-0}{5}=3.\n$$\n\nWe can approximate the integral above using a *right* Riemann sum with $5$ equal subintervals and step size $Δx$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\pi {\\int }_{0}^{15}g(x)\\,\\text{d}x≈\\pi \\cdot (g(3)+g(6)+g(9)+g(12)+g(15))\\cdot Δx\n$$\n\nWe set up a table with values of $g(x)$ at each point:\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $3$ | $6$ | $9$ | $12$ | $15$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x)$ | $3$ | $2$ | $\\sqrt{3}$ | $0$ | $2\\sqrt{2}$ | $1$ |\n| $g(x)={(f(x))}^{2}$ | $9$ | $4$ | $3$ | $0$ | $8$ | $1$ |\n\nFinally, we obtain the following approximation for our volume:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & =\\pi {\\int }_{0}^{15}g(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ≈\\pi \\cdot (g(3)+g(6)+g(9)+g(12)+g(15))\\cdot Δx \\\\  & =\\pi \\cdot (4+3+0+8+1)\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =\\pi \\cdot 16\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =48\\pi \\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
